          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "The Skyrme-Faddeev model involves a map $\\mbox{\\boldmath $\\phi$}: \\hbox{\\mybb R}^3\\mapsto S^2,$ which is realized as a real three-component vector $\\mbox{\\boldmath $\\phi$}=(\\phi_1,\\phi_2,\\phi_3),$ of unit length, $\\mbox{\\boldmath $\\phi$}\\cdot\\mbox{\\boldmath $\\phi$}=1.$ As this paper is concerned only with static solutions then the model can be defined by its energy $$E=\\frac{1}{32\\pi^2\\sqrt{2}}\\int",
      "extractCut": true
    },
